 "about_text": "ATLA is a contemporary gallery in Los Angeles focused on craft-based work, particularly ceramics, that brings together East and West artistic traditions. Its program explores themes of intersectionality, history, heritage, politics, and identity through skilled making. The gallery's name references the Japanese word 'atara,' evoking the sorrow of losing something beautiful, and reflects ATLA's commitment to celebrating endurance and resisting disposability of work, experience, and attention. The gallery operates from a space on Kenmore Avenue and presents exhibitions featuring a wide roster of ceramic and multidisciplinary artists.",
